0	section	Freeing the Homunculus
0	section	Returning to it
1	line	Player	Hello?
1	line	Homunculus	Leeet mwwe free. Argyyghh.
1	line	Player	It's okay, I'm here to help you.
1	line	Homunculus	Lieees. Grahhh
1	line	Player	No, honest. I helped the alchemists, but I had no idea what their plans involved.
1	line	Homunculus	Arggh, so alchemist create me now I trapped for experiements. But still I confused.
1	line	Player	About what?
1	line	Homunculus	Me see logic, feeeel magic. A mix of the two.
1	line	Player	Hmmm. A creature created of logic and magic.
1	line	Player	Don't fear. I shall fix your mind!
1	line	Homunculus	No so sure it is easy to do. No one canna 'elp. Arghhh.
1	line	Player	Watch me.
1	box	You must now make sense of the Homunculus's mind. Force him to either follow the line of logic or the line of magic.
1	line	Player	You tell me that you're confused, so ask me some questions!
1	line	Homunculus	Ah, please...
1	action	Choosing any one of the three options will give three new options in the same order and change the Homunculus' sanity meter. They will eventually loop.
1	cond	First set:
2	select	How can I make fire appear at my fingertips?
2	option	Get some logs and a tinderbox.
2	option	With the aid of 5 fire runes.
2	option	That's impossible! No one can do that!
1	cond	Second set:
2	select	How do dragons breathe fire?
2	option	Not too sure, I've never seen it happen.
2	option	With the help of the magical dragonstones!
2	option	By ignition of gas in their belly as they exhale.
1	cond	Fourth set:
2	select	What do people do, day-in, day-out?
2	option	Runecraft, enchant jewellery, perform alchemy.
2	option	Eat, sleep, nothing that exciting.
2	option	Fletching, Crafting, Smithing.
1	cond	Fifth set:
2	select	What could I do with unwanted bones?
2	option	Bury them.
2	option	I'd like to think you wouldn't be carrying bones around.
2	option	Turn them into bananas or peaches!
1	cond	Sixth set:
2	select	What's the best way to travel?
2	option	I'm not really much of a traveller, sorry.
2	option	Run, run as fast as you can.
2	option	Depends where you are headed, but teleport spells are a safe bet.
1	cond	Seventh set:
2	select	I hear people whisper of potions...
2	option	Yes, you can make magic potions to boost your skills.
2	option	People mix together ingredients in vials. The nutrients will help you.
2	option	Yes, liquid-filled vials. Big deal.
1	cond	Eighth set:
2	select	How are runes created?
2	option	By harnessing the power of the gods!
2	option	Never seen one personally.
2	option	Take some essence to an altar and use a talisman.
1	cond	Ninth set:
2	select	Can people move things with the power of the mind?
2	option	Perhaps. I've never seen it myself, though.
2	option	Yep, you can use the Telekinetic Grab spell.
2	option	Sure. Use your brain to tell someone to move it!
1	cond	Tenth set:
2	select	How can I possibly exist?
2	option	Through the power of alchemy.
2	option	It's beyond me!
2	option	It's a simple case of combining materials.
1	cond	Eleventh set:
2	select	Explain those flashing sparks that scared the alchemists.
2	option	You have special powers - no surprise seeing how you were created.
2	option	Coincidence - there is a lot of loose metal around.
2	option	Yeah, they were cool! Nice one.
1	cond	Twelfth set:
2	select	I want to learn more - what should I study?
2	option	Try some Mining followed by Smithing.
2	option	How about Magic and Runecrafting?
2	option	That's up to you; depends on what you find interesting.
1	cond	Thirteenth set:
2	select	If I can reach out far enough I can grab the sun.
2	option	Don't be silly! You'd get burnt!
2	option	Can't see why not, anything is possible.
2	option	Well the sun is not actually there, it's where it used to be!
1	cond	Fourteenth set:
2	select	Am I a creature of magic or a creature of logic?
2	option	Everything has a reason, even if you don't know what it is.
2	option	Probably a bit of both.
2	option	Your very existense speaks of mystical forces.
1	cond	Fifteenth set:
2	select	Which do you believe in?
2	option	Magic.
2	option	I'm too laid back to really care, mate.
2	option	Logic.
1	action	When the Homunculus' mind is fixed:
1	line	Homunculus	That it! Make sense now, thank you!
1	line	Player	I decided to root for magic.
1	line	Homunculus	No does matter which you chose. Me needed organise my thoughts. I see there is truth in both.
1	line	Player	Okay.
1	line	Homunculus	Now we go scare alchemies - they have been wrong to do this! Although I have life, they mustn't go about this again.
1	line	Player	Sounds like a good plan. Can you get out of that cage?
1	line	Homunculus	Easy. You run down and I watching from here. I surprise right moment.
1	line	Player	Okay.
1	action	end
